    "status": "present",
    "value": "Expand nested brace unions and concatenations into distinct lexicographically sorted words. The approach is: recursive-descent union/concatenation grammar over sets of words. Its target cost is output/intermediate-set-sensitive time and memory; final lexicographic sort. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
